"""Publish compact retrospective receipts; no fitting or seed runs."""
import json,sys,time,hashlib
from pathlib import Path
def main():
    start=time.process_time();store=Path(sys.argv[1]);out=Path(sys.argv[2]);out.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
    d=json.loads((store/'diagnostics.json').read_text());lines=['# Issue 49 Phase A — public context and optimization diagnostics','','Study only. No merge or model promotion. No generated source owners, Q continuations, model fitting, fresh A20 runs, or Issue 48 results were used.','',
    '## Functional evidence','','Initial weights are reconstructed from the selected checkpoint seed and exact original initializer. Selected checkpoints remain unchanged. Every one of the 512 derivative inputs is matched byte-hash to its sealed #47 receipt and Q/serialized content to its sealed #46 source table. Scores use float64, one Torch thread. MSE is against Q/60 with equal root then equal option weights. Q regret is in native floor units. Old heldout is retrospective, not an untouched new test.','',
    '| Model | Split | Initial/selected Q regret | Argmax agreement | Initial/selected score margin | Initial/selected centered MSE |','|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
    for name,m in d['models'].items():
        for r in m['partition_metrics']:
            if r['family']=='ALL':lines.append(f"| {name} | {r['split']} | {r['initial_regret']:.6g} / {r['selected_regret']:.6g} | {r['argmax_agreement']:.6g} | {r['initial_margin']:.6g} / {r['selected_margin']:.6g} | {r['initial_centered_mse']:.6g} / {r['selected_centered_mse']:.6g} |")
    lines+=['','Complete family/provenance cells and per-root metrics are in diagnostics.json and per-root.json. Natural MAP and assisted REWARDS are absent in both old validation and heldout; do not infer balanced deployment generalization. Training has 96 roots in each of four cells.','', '## Absolute floor fit versus action ranking','','| Model | Actual training roots MSE, initial → selected |','|---|---|']
    for name,m in d['models'].items():lines.append(f"| {name} | {m['initial_actual_training_mse']:.9g} → {m['selected_actual_training_mse']:.9g} |")
    lines+=['','S models use their actual 96-owner training subset for this MSE; partition rows describe all historical roots, including 288 training-labelled roots outside S fitting. #46 Bigger did learn substantial common floor prediction. Small parameter displacement alone does not establish lack of training. Action regret, centered score changes and concordance must be examined independently.','', '## Preference gradients','','| Objective | Full gradient L2 | Cancellation ratio | Mean root cosine | Pair logistic derivative mean | Hypothetical SGD0.01 centered score-change RMS |','|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
    for name in ('47/A','47/P'):
        g=d['models'][name]['epoch0_gradient'];lines.append(f"| {name} | {g['full_batch_l2']:.9g} | {g['cancellation_ratio_norm_mean_over_mean_norm']:.9g} | {g['mean_pairwise_root_gradient_cosine']:.9g} | {g['logistic_derivative']['mean']:.9g} | {g['hypothetical_one_SGD001_centered_score_change']['rms']:.9g} |")
    lines+=['','P gradients do not vanish: the output bias cancels exactly (floating error ~1e-18), hidden bias gradients are small, and the informative-root average retains about 13% of the mean root-gradient norm. Logistic derivatives remain near −0.5, not saturated. Small action-difference gradients, partial root cancellation and SGD0.01 jointly produce very small centered score movement. This receipt supports slow accumulation under the frozen objective; it does not uniquely establish a causal optimizer defect. Existing first/final objective records are preserved alongside layer norms. The hypothetical direction is evaluated once and restored immediately; no model is fitted or saved.','',
    '## Public-v2 prototype and limitations','','The normalizer binds card fields within each entity, retains all currently projected legal offers, canonicalizes mutually exclusive groups, and uses public local group/card content keys. Native indices establish public grouping before they are stripped; opaque executor fields do not enter features. Duplicates retain multiplicity. Exact semantic and candidate×context tokens demonstrate representability and reorder equivariance without selecting a neural architecture or implying learned strategic quality. Full public_state is retained from the trusted adapter; arbitrary nested objects supplied by an untrusted caller are outside this contract.','',
    'Complete normal-player observation equivalence is not established: pinned reward projection omits misc and exact upgrade_count, whose inspectability relevance needs further source-public contract review. Unavailable fields cannot be recovered by the normalizer. See visibility.md for exact reward-field gaps and transition caveats. Unknown hidden RNG/top-level future content is excluded; no post-action future facts are backfilled. Honest synthetic public fixtures are not game-strength evidence.','',
    '## Recommended single next treatment for Planner approval','','After resolving the source-public snapshot gaps documented by the audit, prescribe one complete current-public choice-set conditioning treatment with explicit group/entity pointers versus the unchanged frozen baseline. Freeze its optimizer and function-space learning thresholds prospectively, with balanced natural/assisted × MAP/REWARDS validation owners. Keep labels, Battle controller and all other treatment choices fixed. No Phase B fitting or complete-run comparison is authorized here; no winner or new cohort is selected.','',
    '## Reproduction','','Use Python 3.13 Torch 2.12.0+cpu for diagnose.py and verify_gradients.py; system Python 3.14 for prototype/native checks. Commands accept an independent output directory; original stores remain read-only. Native harness uses explicitly synthetic default GameContext data and pinned source transitions, never a seeded game constructor.','',
    '```text','python diagnose.py /home/lsmft/.cache/issue49-public-diagnostics','python verify_gradients.py /home/lsmft/.cache/issue49-public-diagnostics','python test_prototype.py /home/lsmft/.cache/issue49-public-diagnostics','```','']
    (out/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines));print({'cpu_seconds':time.process_time()-start})
if __name__=='__main__':main()
